{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q867332","formula":"C₁₇H₂₅NO₃","hill":"C17H25NO3","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":17.0,"H":25.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0},"names":{"en":"Cyclopentolate-(RS)","ru":"Циклопентолат"},"descriptions":{"en":"Cyclopentolate is a muscarinic antagonist. It is commonly used as an eye drop during pediatric eye examinations to dilate the eye (mydriatic) and prevent the eye from focusing/accommodating (cycloplegic). Cyclopentolate or atropine can also be administered to reverse muscarinic and central nervous system effects of indirect cholinomimetic (anti-AChase) administration.","ru":"Циклопентола́т, или цикломе́д (лат. Cyclopentolatum, род. Cyclopentolati) — это синтетический психотропный лекарственный препарат короткого действия, входящий в перечень лекарственных средств для медицинского применения, подлежащих предметно-количественному учёту в Российской Федерации."},"fame":19,"pubchemCid":2905,"mass":291.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN(C)CCOC(=O)C(C1=CC=CC=C1)C2(CCCC2)O","inchikey":"SKYSRIRYMSLOIN-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(dimethylamino)ethyl 2-(1-hydroxycyclopentyl)-2-phenylacetate","classes":[{"qid":"Q59199015","names":{"en":"group of stereoisomers","ru":"группа стереоизомеров","uk":"група стереоізомерів"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"2905","atoms":46,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":2.292,"y":-1.049,"z":1.377,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.557,"y":-0.096,"z":-0.281,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.539,"y":-0.925,"z":1.611,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.233,"y":0.077,"z":-0.032,"el":"N"},{"x":1.861,"y":-1.274,"z":0.035,"el":"C"},{"x":3.078,"y":-1.226,"z":-0.886,"el":"C"},{"x":1.384,"y":-2.716,"z":-0.119,"el":"C"},{"x":3.758,"y":-2.58,"z":-0.683,"el":"C"},{"x":2.675,"y":-3.532,"z":-0.175,"el":"C"},{"x":0.801,"y":-0.244,"z":-0.321,"el":"C"},{"x":1.297,"y":1.188,"z":-0.161,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.482,"y":-0.479,"z":0.472,"el":"C"},{"x":1.998,"y":1.769,"z":-1.197,"el":"C"},{"x":1.03,"y":1.857,"z":1.015,"